      "writtenOn": "2020-02-05T10:53:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a hypothetical question. Because we never had deep hierarchies in schedtune in Android.\n\nwe are enforcing the hold value to be greater than its parent. however the child may have lower than the newly written value.\n\nLets say\n\nroot \u003d 0 msec\n\n/root/A is created and /root/A hold is set to 10 msec\n\n/root/A/B is created. By default root/A/B hold get 10 msec\n\nNow what happens if we write 15 msec to /root/A . we will allow it because it is greater than root\u0027s hold i.e 0. With this A (parent) have more value than the child B",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7429,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7429,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "db576960014cfd26b0e869d0763b4cc847c12933",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10dad051_6753378b",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/core.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 7429,
      "author": {
        "id": 1456182
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-05T12:29:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is a very good question. We do have a bug in this area you\u0027re right. We don\u0027t have a function to update the hierarchy when a value changes.\n\nHmm this means we need to keep track of the original group request and the effective (real one) based on hierarchy restrictions.",
      "parentUuid": "758207fc_f77e73e9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7429,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7429,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "db576960014cfd26b0e869d0763b4cc847c12933",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e94110b0_4324df50",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/core.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 7429,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291841
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-05T15:44:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "And that\u0027s why we have two concepts: requested values -vs- effective values.\n\nWhen it comes to cpu.util.{min,max}, each cgroup tracks its requested value and we do a hierarchical update on write in cpu_util_update_eff():\n   https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/latest/source/kernel/sched/core.c#L7181\n\nThe same logic should apply for the boot hold propagation.",
      "parentUuid": "10dad051_6753378b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7429,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7429,
        "endChar": 1
      },
